  "prefLabel": "Plc 1001.01 Purpose",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1001.01 Purpose. The purpose of this chapter is to:\n\n(a) In Plc 1001, establish the fees charged by the office of professional licensure and certification (OPLC) that are related to:\n\n(1) Services provided by or for the OPLC and by or for:\n\na. The boards listed in RSA 310:2, II, hereinafter referred to as “supported boards”; and\n\nb. The professions listed in RSA 310:2, II that do not have an associated board;\n\n(2) Inspections, including inspections related to licensure and inspections not related to licensure;\n\n(3) Obtaining approval from a supported board for a candidate supervision agreement, where such approval is required by applicable law;\n\n(4) Obtaining approval from a supported board for a continuing competence provider, program, or instructor, where such approval is required by appliable law based on an application being submitted to the board for review and a decision regarding whether to approve a specific provider, program, or instructor;\n\n(5) Audits of continuing competence activities and records; and\n\n(6) Attending a board-sponsored program;\n\n(b) In Plc 1002, establish the fees charged by the OPLC for application processing and licensing;\n\n(c) In Plc 1003, establish the process for paying per diems and providing reimbursements to board members; and\n\n(d) In Plc 1004, establish fees for the various examinations required for licensure.\n\nSource. #13264, INTERIM, eff 9-22-21; ss by #13336, eff 1-27-22; ss by #13838, eff 1-26-24; ss by #14289, eff 7-1-25, EXPIRES: 7-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1000.html"
